rer.md:41:## Why SVG for now\ndocs/decisions/0002-mark-renderer.md:47:## What this does not establish\ndocs/decisions/0002-mark-renderer.md:55:## Consequences\ndocs/01-landscape.md:1:# Phase 1a: the browser charting landscape, November 2026\ndocs/01-landscape.md:5:## Summary\ndocs/01-landscape.md:24:## 1. Which libraries, and how sure can we be\ndocs/01-landscape.md:26:### 1.1 Adoption data\ndocs/01-landscape.md:57:### 1.2 What these numbers cannot tell us\ndocs/01-landscape.md:71:### 1.3 The ten: a chosen sample, not a ranking\ndocs/01-landscape.md:95:### 1.4 Maintenance and cost facts\ndocs/01-landscape.md:99:| Chart.js | 4.6.1 | 2026-10-22 | 1 | none | MIT | 81 KiB | 54 |\ndocs/01-landscape.md:100:| Recharts | 3.11.0 | 2026-11-17 | 12 | v3 (2025-06) | MIT | 140 KiB + React | 83 + 9 shared |\ndocs/01-landscape.md:101:| D3 | 7.9.2 | 2026-11-03 | 2 | none | ISC | 35 KiB | 91 |\ndocs/01-landscape.md:102:| ECharts | 6.1.0 | 2026-05-19 | 1 | v6 (2025-07) | Apache-2.0 | 373 KiB | 63 |\ndocs/01-landscape.md:103:| Highcharts | 13.1.1 | 2026-09-20 | 10 | v12 (2024-11), v13 (2026-06) | Commercial | 143 KiB, accessibility module included | 51 |\ndocs/01-landscape.md:104:| ApexCharts | 8.9.0 | 2026-11-17 | 65 | v5 (2025-07), v6 (2026-07), v7 (2026-08), v8 (2026-10) | Free below a size threshold, otherwise commercial | 289 KiB | 60 |\ndocs/01-landscape.md:105:| Plotly.js | 4.3.0 | 2026-11-10 | 12 | v3 (2025-01), v4 (2026-08) | MIT | 1,450 KiB | 30 |\ndocs/01-landscape.md:106:| Nivo | 0.99.0 | 2025-05-23 | 0 | none | MIT | 129 KiB + React | 54 + 9 shared |\ndocs/01-landscape.md:107:| MUI X Charts | 9.18.1 | 2026-11-16 | 43 | v8 (2025-04), v9 (2026-04) | MIT; zoom and pan need the Pro plan | 160 KiB + React | 44 + 9 shared |\ndocs/01-landscape.md:108:| uPlot | 1.6.32 | 2025-03-14 | 0 | none | MIT | 23 KiB, no donut | 45 |\ndocs/01-landscape.md:112:## 2. Method\ndocs/01-landscape.md:142:## 3. How the charts look and communicate\ndocs/01-landscape.md:146:### 3.1 Scoreboard\ndocs/01-landscape.md:162:### 3.2 Findings\ndocs/01-landscape.md:248:## 4. How readers explore and interact\ndocs/01-landscape.md:250:### 4.1 Scoreboard\ndocs/01-landscape.md:268:### 4.2 Findings\ndocs/01-landscape.md:290:### 4.3 Accessibility with each library's switch off and on\ndocs/01-landscape.md:304:## 5. How developers create, update and maintain\ndocs/01-landscape.md:308:### 5.1 What each library needed beyond data\ndocs/01-landscape.md:320:| Plotly.js | Nothing extra. The shortest module, and 1,450 KiB gzipped with the documented import. |\ndocs/01-landscape.md:325:### 5.2 Findings\ndocs/01-landscape.md:333:**D4. Bundle cost spans a wide range** with the documented imports: 23 KiB to 1,450 KiB gzipped for the harness modules (section 1.4, with its caveats).\ndocs/01-landscape.md:341:### 5.3 Load\ndocs/01-landscape.md:384:## 6. What the findings add up to\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:1:# Phase 2 plan: Axylo 1.0 in TypeScript\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:9:## 1. Public API\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:13:### 1.1 Shape\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:38:### 1.2 Data: one logical table, three forms\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:63:### 1.3 Fields\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:90:### 1.4 Common options\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:107:### 1.5 Handle and commit contract\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:130:### 1.6 Diagnostics\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:143:The reader of that chart sees \"Values not shown: 3. See table.\" (F12).\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:149:### 1.7 React adapter\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:167:## 2. Architecture\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:169:### 2.1 Pipeline\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:190:### 2.2 Invalidation\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:204:### 2.3 Rendering\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:216:### 2.4 Document structure\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:239:### 2.5 Repository\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:255:## 3. Milestones\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:259:### M0. Foundations (ceiling: 5 days)\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:268:### M1. A vertical slice, and the two open decisions (ceiling: 12 days)\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:284:### M2. Faithful data, on the line chart (ceiling: 8 days)\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:286:- The diagnostic registry (F3, F12); missing values and absent steps (F2); the three temporal types (F4); formatting (F6); domains (F7); sorting and duplicates (F11); `validate()`.\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:296:### M3. Reading the chart (ceiling: 10 days)\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:309:### M4. Accessibility, complete on the line chart (ceiling: 10 days)\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:322:### M5. Bar, area, donut, scatter and the compact variant (ceiling: 18 days)\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:336:### M6. Updates and scale (ceiling: 10 days)\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:348:### M7. Distribution and documentation (ceiling: 8 days)\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:355:- Size measured on the packed distribution for line-only, full, script-tag and React cases, CSS included (DX7).\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:359:### M8. Release (ceiling: 10 days)\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:370:## 4. Test strategy\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:381:| Packed distribution | Clean install fixtures | What users actually get (DX1, DX7, DX8, DX10). |\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:386:## 5. Risks\ndocs/03-plan-typescript-release.md:398:## 6. What waits until after 1.0\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:1:# Phase 1b: Axylo product specification\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:7:## 1. What Axylo is\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:15:### 1.1 Why someone would choose it\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:29:### 1.2 Who it is for\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:35:### 1.3 Principles\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:46:## 2. Scope of the first release\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:48:### 2.1 Chart types\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:65:### 2.2 Workflows\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:76:### 2.3 Supported environments\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:86:## 3. Acceptance criteria: the reader's experience\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:90:### 3.1 Faithful representation\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:105:| F12 | When a warning means values were left out or changed, the chart says so to the reader: a short note (\"Values not shown: 2. See table.\", worded so it reads correctly for any count) inside the figure and in the accessibility tree, in every build. | Production build given `dirty` shows the note | R5, R6 |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:107:### 3.2 Legibility\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:120:### 3.3 Interaction\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:131:### 3.4 Accessibility\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:148:### 3.5 Diagnostic registry\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:150:Level decides delivery. **Error**: the chart or a series cannot be drawn; the chart shows its error state. **Warning**: something is not drawn as given; the reader sees the note in F12. **Hint**: advice for the author. Errors and warnings print once per code per page in every build; hints print in development builds only. `strict: true` throws on errors and warnings found while validating a create, `update` or `append` call, synchronously from that call. A diagnostic that can only arise later (a contrast check after the page's CSS changes, a custom formatter that throws when a table page is built, a label that stops fitting after a resize) is reported when it is found and is never thrown. Every diagnostic names the chart; those about data name the field and the first row indexes in the caller's own data.\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:184:Expected results for the Phase 1 fixtures: the combined `dirty` fixture (`[10, 20, null, NaN, '40', undefined, 70]`) yields AX102, AX103 and AX106 once each, draws Mon–Tue as a segment and Sun as a point, and shows the F12 note. `dirty-string` (one `'40'` among numbers) yields AX106. A column made only of numeric strings yields AX104 and is drawn in full. `dirty-null` yields nothing.\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:188:### 3.6 Type matrix\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:200:### 3.7 Compact variant\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:210:| C5 | When values were left out (F12), the description says so and a small marker with a text equivalent appears in the corner. | `dirty` fixture in compact mode |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:214:### 3.8 What the evidence will and will not show\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:218:## 4. Acceptance criteria: the developer's experience\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:228:| DX7 | Zero runtime dependencies (reconsidered only with a measured comparison). Size targets, provisional until M1 measures a working slice: 40 KiB gzipped for everything, 25 KiB for a page that uses only `line`, 2 KiB for the React adapter, CSS included. | size-limit in CI on the packed distribution | D4 |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:235:## 5. Performance budgets\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:246:| P6 | Download | Minified and gzipped bytes, CSS included | Exact | DX7 | 01, section 1.4 |\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:256:## 6. Decisions and the findings behind them\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:281:## 7. Changes this revision rejected\ndocs/02-product-spec.md:290:## 8. Decisions still open\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
