{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba acceptance/README.md && nl -ba reviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/dist.report.md | sed -n '31,84p' && rg -n '1,216|1216|494' reviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/*report.md\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t# Release acceptance\n     2\t\n     3\tFrom the repository root\n     4\t\n     5\t```sh\n     6\tnode --test acceptance/test/*.test.mjs\n     7\tnode acceptance/check.mjs\n     8\tmkdir -p acceptance/results\n     9\tenv -u AXYLO_BROWSER timeout 120 npx vitest run --reporter=json --outputFile=acceptance/results/unit.json\n    10\tnode acceptance/check.mjs --results acceptance/results/unit.json\n    11\tnode acceptance/check.mjs --release --results acceptance/results/unit.json\n    12\t```\n    13\t\n    14\tSupply any number of Vitest JSON reports after `--results`, including browser reports collected on a machine that can run them. The checker prints the table and rewrites [report.md](report.md). Structural errors always exit 1. With `--release`, any `fail` or `no evidence` also exits 1. Review the other open statuses before tagging a release.\n    15\t\n    16\t| Status | Meaning |\n    17\t|---|---|\n    18\t| pass | Every required test has a passing assertion result. |\n    19\t| fail | At least one required test failed in a supplied report. |\n    20\t| no evidence | The criterion applies and has no qualifying evidence. Weak checks appear in the gap list. |\n    21\t| not run | Required results are absent or skipped, or a provisional budget has no matching measurement. |\n    22\t| cannot be verified here | A required environment or rehearsal is unavailable, or an archived measurement has no frozen limit to compare against. The report links measured history without a verdict. |\n    23\t| not applicable | The criterion does not apply to this type. The cell gives the reason. |\n    24\t\n    25\tFirefox, Safari/WebKit, native phone behavior, screen-reader rehearsal and hardware GPU rasterisation cannot be verified here. The cited benchmark records use software rasterisation and measure main-thread work. Hardware rasterisation has no pass/fail budget of its own in spec §5.\n    26\t\n    27\t## Add a row\n    28\t\n    29\tUse the ID and short wording from the spec. Section 3.6 cells use `T-<rule>-<chart type>`. Add an `appliesTo` list and give a `notApplicable` reason for every excluded type. Negative type-matrix cells such as “No” zoom are applicable checks of absence. The compact column covers the variant defined in §3.7.\n    30\t\n    31\tRead each test body and file it under the chart type it actually exercises. An `evidence` item takes a repository-relative `file` and a `kind` of `unit`, `property`, `browser`, `benchmark`, `document` or `manual rehearsal`. For tests use the exact Vitest `title` or a `prefix` of a `describe` title when the entire suite is needed. Add a `reason` to each `weak` item. Benchmark entries take a `workload` and optional `history` paths. Use `cannotVerify` for environmental limits and `pending` for provisional work, with reasons by type.\n    32\t\n    33\tThe source scanner checks conventional registrations and simple parameterized titles without importing tests. Its limits are documented in [titles.mjs](titles.mjs). A failed assertion takes precedence across reports. Documents, manual notes and provisional benchmark measurements require review outside the Vitest result join.\n    31\t### What ran (all observed)\n    32\t- Node, `npx vitest run --config tests/dist/vitest.config.ts`: `Test Files 8 passed (8) / Tests 83 passed (83)`.\n    33\t- Browser, `AXYLO_BROWSER=1 npx vitest run --config tests/dist/vitest.config.ts`: `Test Files 2 passed (2) / Tests 18 passed (18)`.\n    34\t- `npx tsc -p tests/dist`: exit 0.\n    35\t- `packages/react/test/dist.test.ts`: still 12/12 after the metadata changes.\n    36\t\n    37\tWhat each group shows:\n    38\t- **Isolation:** the fixture packages are real directories, not links. Node (with and without `--conditions=development`) and esbuild resolve `axylo`, `axylo/axylo.css`, `@axylo/react`, and the adapter's own `import 'axylo'`, to fixture paths only. A control assertion confirms the root `node_modules/axylo` really does link to the workspace, so the check has something to catch.\n    39\t- **Package contents:** every `exports` target under every condition, and every `files` entry, is in the tarball. Nothing else ships beyond the declarations the types entries import, the two IIFE files, README, LICENSE and package.json. No source, tests or source maps; declarations import only peer dependencies.\n    40\t- **Types:** strict `tsc` with `skipLibCheck: false` passes on a consumer file and on each snippet, in both fixtures. `--listFiles` shows the declarations came from the fixture. The `@ts-expect-error` lines for the DX3 mistakes behave correctly, so the declarations are real types, not `any`.\n    41\t- **Conditions:** `development` and the default are different files in Node and in esbuild, and neither contains `__DEV__`.\n    42\t  - How I checked for development-only code: I found every `if (__DEV__) …` in the source and bundled the source twice, once as is and once with those statements cut out. Text present only in the first bundle counts as development-only.\n    43\t  - Found for `axylo`: `__dev`, `stages`, `retainedRows`. For `@axylo/react`: `[axylo/react] <`, `> was given `, `columns`.\n    44\t  - Each is present in the packed development file and absent from the production one.\n    45\t  - In the browser, the AX104 hint prints once in the development flavour and not at all in production.\n    46\t- **Side effects:** importing either package and using nothing bundles to 0 bytes. Importing `axylo` in Node adds no globals, and in Chrome it leaves the document untouched. `import 'axylo/axylo.css'` survives bundling.\n    47\t- **DX8 in Node:**\n    48\t  - Importing `axylo` works without DOM globals.\n    49\t  - `validate()` on the Phase 1 dirty fixture returns exactly AX102 (row 5), AX103 (row 3) and AX106 (row 4), as spec 3.5 and plan 1.6 say.\n    50\t  - `line('#nowhere')` with no document throws a message naming `#nowhere`.\n    51\t  - Server rendering of the snippet and all five components gives an empty `<div>` container each.\n    52\t- **DX1 in Chrome:**\n    53\t  - The npm snippet (production and development conditions), the script-tag snippet and the React snippet under StrictMode each draw one figure named \"Monthly visitors\" with series-painted marks, and print no console error or warning.\n    54\t  - Hydrating the server markup produces no mismatch.\n    55\t  - Without `title`, the chart still draws and raises only AX140.\n    56\t- **DX8 under CSP:** 8 page variants: {IIFE min, IIFE dev, bundled module prod, bundled module dev} × {stylesheet applied at run time, stylesheet linked by the page}. Each draws all five chart types plus the compact variant and opens tooltips and all five tables. Result: zero violation events, zero reports, zero console errors, no elements created from `<img onerror>` or `<script>` text in titles, series, categories, labels, units or formatters, and `#no-such-chart` is named in the thrown error. Run-time styling adopts exactly one sheet; the linked case adopts none; there are never any `<style>` elements. A negative control (an `insertAdjacentHTML` page) is caught by both instruments.\n    57\t  - The exact policy: `default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; report-uri /csp-report`\n    58\t- **DX11:** MIT field and LICENSE text in both packages. No runtime dependencies. The shipped JS imports nothing, except `react` and `axylo` from the adapter. Bundling each package's source with the release settings reads only its own `src`, so no `node_modules` code is compiled in. No licence headers in `packages/*/src` or in the shipped files.\n    59\t\n    60\t### Sizes (`node scripts/size.mjs`, from the packed files, esbuild minify, production condition, gzip level 9)\n    61\t\n    62\t| entry | min B | js gzip B | css file gzip B | total KiB | target KiB | status |\n    63\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n    64\t| line only (`npm.ts`) | 282,947 | 99,956 | — | 97.61 | 25 | OVER |\n    65\t| everything | 283,389 | 100,093 | — | 97.75 | 40 | OVER |\n    66\t| script tag (IIFE min + css) | 283,869 | 100,179 | 4,095 | 101.83 | — | no target |\n    67\t| React adapter alone | 2,375 | 1,197 | — | 1.17 | 2 | ok |\n    68\t\n    69\t- `--check` exits 1.\n    70\t- The JS already carries the stylesheet string, so the bundler rows do not add the CSS file. Adding it, as the old script did, would add 4,095 B.\n    71\t- Breakdown by directory (minified bytes): data 24.3%, core 16.1%, dom 13.5%, theme 8.8%. Largest modules: `core/controller.ts`, `dom/interaction.ts`, `data/store.ts`, `theme/css.ts`.\n    72\t- A rebuild from source with the release settings is byte-identical in size to the packed `axylo.js`.\n    73\t- **Finding: chart types do not tree-shake.** Line-only saves 137 B gzip compared with everything. Building from source gives the same result (line-only 99,735 B, everything 99,912 B, `validate` only 20,686 B).\n    74\t  - The likely cause (inferred, not proven) is that every chart function goes through `createChart(type, …)` in `packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts` / `core/controller.ts`, which reaches all types.\n    75\t\n    76\t### Failing tests\n    77\tNone among the 101. The only failure is `size.mjs --check`, above, for DX7.\n    78\t\n    79\t### Where the spec was ambiguous, and what I assumed\n    80\t1. **DX1 options:** \"no option besides data and fields\" conflicts with AX140, which is a warning (spec 3.5), and with \"no console warnings\". The snippets therefore pass `title`, as the plan 1.1 example does. A test shows the title is not required. `acceptance/matrix.json` DX1 still says \"only data and fields\".\n    81\t2. **Script-tag file names:** plan 1.6 calls the script-tag files `axylo.js`/`axylo.min.js`. The build produces `axylo.iife.js`/`axylo.iife.min.js`, and `axylo.js` is the production ESM file. The snippet uses `dist/axylo.iife.min.js`.\n    82\t3. **Script-tag URL:** the snippet uses unversioned `https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/axylo/dist/...` for a package not yet published. The test routes those URLs to the packed files.\n    83\t4. **Script-tag target:** the spec gives no size target for the script-tag row.\n    84\t5. **React snippet shape:** it exports a component, which the fixture's `main.tsx` mounts.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/acceptance-node.report.md:3:Added **494 Node acceptance tests** across 16 files. They exercise all 29 diagnostic codes and provide model evidence for 224 applicable matrix cells. All edits are under `packages/axylo/test/acceptance/`. No contract changes are needed.\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/acceptance-node.report.md:17:      Tests  18 failed | 476 passed (494)\nreviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/core3.fix.report.md:96:- **Node core:** `Tests 114 passed (114)`. Node acceptance: `Tests 494 passed (494)`.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
