eight; otherwise it is as tall as its content. */\n   113\t  .axylo-figure {\n   114\t    position: relative; display: flex; flex-direction: column; box-sizing: border-box;\n   115\t    margin: 0; padding: 0; height: 100%; min-width: 0; min-height: 0;\n2: * The library's default stylesheet as a string. `ensureStyles` adopts it as a constructable stylesheet; the\n70:  .axylo .axylo-svg, .axylo .axylo-canvas { position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0; display: block; pointer-events: none; }\n72:  .axylo .axylo-canvas > canvas { position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0; display: block; }\n75:   * Dash patterns of the SVG renderer. Each dashed element carries its normal pattern inline and both\n76:   * patterns as custom properties; this switch needs no redraw (spec A5).\n133:  /* The plot's column: the plot, and the open table over it. */\n137:  .axylo-compact .axylo-plot::before { aspect-ratio: auto; min-height: 0; max-height: none; height: 32px; }\n149:  .axylo .axylo-tooltip, .axylo .axylo-readout {\n155:  /* The fixed readout under the plot of a narrow tile (spec I1): it overlays what is below, so showing it\n157:  .axylo .axylo-readout { right: 0; max-width: none; }\n182:   * two-finger pan come to the chart. Tick text is not selectable, so a drag selects a range, not text.\n187:  /* The keyboard proxy (decision 0001): a native range over the plot, transparent, never in the pointer's way. */\n188:  .axylo .axylo-proxy {\n198:  .axylo .axylo-proxy:focus-visible + .axylo-focus-ring { display: block; }\n199:  /* The donut slice the keyboard is on, also when it has no arc. */\n207:  /* Legend, toolbar and table, under the plot. */\n209:  /* legend: 'top' puts the legend and its toolbar above the plot; 'right' beside it, entries stacked. */\n236:  .axylo .axylo-table { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.5em; min-width: 0; }\n237:  /* The open table takes the plot's place at the plot's size, so nothing else moves (spec A4; review 2, finding 15). */\n238:  .axylo .axylo